  "thag21.1:63.3": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Kāmakāro</i>: “wish-granter”. Ordinary people cannot simply get what they want. ",
  "thag21.1:63.4": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Saṅkheyyakāro</i>: “comprehensibility-granter”. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Saṅkheyya</i> is “calculable, comprehensible”, not “after comprehension”. The Buddha has a gift for explaining things in a way that makes them comprehensible. ",
